w: 1.~O Lord, thou hast been fa- vo- rable to thy be- lov- ed land: Ja- cob's cap- ti- vi- ty thou hast re- called with might- y hand.
w: 2.~Thou par- don- èd thy peo- ple hast all their i- ni- qui- ties; Thou all their tre- spas- ses and sins hast co- vered from thine eyes.
w: 3.~Thou took'st off all thine ire, and turn'dst from thy wrath's fu- riou- sness. Turn us, God of our health, and cause thy wrath 'gainst us to cease.
w: 4.~Shall thy dis- plea- sure thus en- dure a- gainst us with- out end? Wilt thou to gen- er- a- tions all thine an- ger forth ex- tend?
w: 5.~That in thee may thy peo- ple joy, wilt thou not us re- vive? Show us thy mer- cy, Lord, to us do thy sal- va- tion give.
w: 6.~I'll hear what God the Lord will speak: to his folk he'll speak peace, And to his saints; but let them not re- turn to foo- lish- ness.
w: 7.~To them that fear him sure- ly near is his sal- va- ti- on; That glo- ry in our land may have her hab- i- ta- ti- on.
w: * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
w: 9.~Yea, what is good the Lord shall give; our land shall yield in- crease: Jus- tice, to set us in his steps, shall go be- fore his face.
